#: Dialogue/error_demoentity.tres
msgid "*Something opened in the barriers of this world*"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/error_demoworld.tres
msgid "You found something out of place"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/error_demoworld.tres
msgid "It stares at you for a long time, before opening its mouth to speak"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/error_demoworld.tres
msgid "It asks you if you've seen its mother"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/error_demoworld.tres
msgid "... Only it didn't speak"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/error_demoworld.tres
msgid "Instead it stared at you, pleadingly, with tears welling in its eyes"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/error_demoworld.tres
msgid "As if waiting for you to understand its peril through body alone"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/error_demoworld.tres
msgid "... But you couldn't, and you shook your head"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/error_demoworld.tres
msgid "Its head lowered towards the floor, wandering away"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/error_demoworld.tres
msgid "Well, not before looking back to you, as if coming to ask you something else"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/error_demoworld.tres
msgid "You couldn't bear another question, so instead you held out your hand, a gift contained within"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/error_demoworld.tres
msgid "*Obtained the Erroneous Glaive*"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/error_demoworld.tres
msgid "And then you parted ways"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/tripdawg.tres
msgid "Don't Even Trip Dawg!"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/tutorial_sign.tres
msgid ""
"Welcome to Midnight Dungeons! This is the dungeon demo, so you'll only get to play the dungeons (two of them). This game is primarily played using both the keyboard and mouse, however there are certain keybinds and features meant to allow for use of one or the other.\n"
"\n"
"Press [[Primary]] to advance dialogue."
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/tutorial_sign.tres
msgid "You can also press [[Secondary]] to instantly complete any dialogue! This acts as a sort of \"skip\". Holding [[Tertiary]] will skip through all dialogue.\n"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/tutorial_sign.tres
msgid "Pressing [[Pause]] will pause the game. Pressing [[Tertiary]] will bring up the RPG menu (this is where your global inventory is). Lastly holding [[Quaternary]] while moving will allow you to sprint."
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/tutorial_sign.tres
msgid "That's all! Have fun playing the game!"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_beta.tres
msgid "Thanks for playing the dungeon demo for Midnight Dungeons!"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid "!!!"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid "Hey there!"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid "Apologies for the frightening entrance, it's just I feel I've seen you before?"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid "...?"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid "Wait, I've got it!"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid "You're that new kid from the guild! Midnight, I believe?"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid ":)"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid "I'll take that as a yes..."
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid "Anyways, name's Stell, but you can just refer to me as the Vendor. I'm usually lurking about these dungeons, selling useful items to any dungeon crawler making their way through."
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid "Normally I'd try my best not to interact with them, but..."
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid "?"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid "we're both shapeshifters, ain't we?"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid "It's not all too often I see another one around!"
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid "... unless it's the ones who've unfortunately lost their autonomy to The Force."
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid "Either way, you've got a lot to learn about this world kid. I'll be here 'til you're out of here."
msgstr ""

#: Dialogue/vendor_intro.tres
msgid "Farewell!"
msgstr ""

